{"id":"sikagard-62-t","rules":[{"id":"sikagard-62-t:restriction:3149f9fa","type":"restriction","polarity":"no","conditional":false,"tags":{},"mentions":[],"text":"Thinner or solvents must not be used.","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/7/sikagard-62-t.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2023, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/concrete-repair-protection/corrosion-management/protective-coatingssilaneimpregnations/sikagard-62-t.html"}},{"id":"sikagard-62-t:product_relation:a891affc","type":"product_relation","polarity":"yes","conditional":true,"tags":{},"mentions":["sikagard-62"],"text":"Do not mix and apply product that has a temperature of greater than 30oC. If applying at higher 30oC, as soon as the Sikagard®-62 T is mixed transfer the container into an esky containing ice to just below the rim of the container, then apply the Sikagard®-62 T from the open container in the esky.","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/7/sikagard-62-t.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2023, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/concrete-repair-protection/corrosion-management/protective-coatingssilaneimpregnations/sikagard-62-t.html"}},{"id":"sikagard-62-t:alternative:29e1e4a6","type":"alternative","polarity":"no","conditional":true,"tags":{},"mentions":["sikagard-62"],"text":"To avoid unslightly water spotting do not apply Sikagard®-62 T when ambient temperature will reach \"dew point\" before the coating has cured.","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/7/sikagard-62-t.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2023, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/concrete-repair-protection/corrosion-management/protective-coatingssilaneimpregnations/sikagard-62-t.html"}},{"id":"sikagard-62-t:alternative:c642745e","type":"alternative","polarity":"no","conditional":false,"tags":{},"mentions":["sikagard-62"],"text":"Do not apply Sikagard®-62 T to cementitious mortars that are modified with acrylic, acrylic co-polymer, EVA or PVA polymers (eg","heading":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/7/sikagard-62-t.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2023, Version 01.02","section":"IMPORTANT CONSIDERATIONS","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/concrete-repair-protection/corrosion-management/protective-coatingssilaneimpregnations/sikagard-62-t.html"}},{"id":"sikagard-62-t:suitability:bad8fc5b","type":"suitability","polarity":"yes","conditional":true,"tags":{"substrate":["cement_render"]},"mentions":[],"text":"The roughness of the substrate needs to be levelled with a suitable Sika® rendering and levelling mortar","heading":"SUBSTRATE PREPARATION","source":{"doc_type":"PDS","url":"https://aus.sika.com/content/dam/dms/au01/7/sikagard-62-t.pdf","page":2,"page_end":2,"doc_version":"April 2023, Version 01.02","section":"SUBSTRATE PREPARATION","web_url":"https://aus.sika.com/en/construction/concrete-repair-protection/corrosion-management/protective-coatingssilaneimpregnations/sikagard-62-t.html"}}]}